## Technical Notes

### OSC Addresses
- Format: `/{receiver_name}`
- Examples: `/frequency`, `/trigger`, `/volume`
- Receivers defined in Pd patch

### Message Types
- **Bang:** Event triggers, no data payload
- **Float:** Numeric values for parameters
- **DSP Toggle:** Audio computation control

### Timing
- Real-time audio processing
- Sample-accurate timing possible
- Low-latency control (< 5ms)

## Common Workflows

### Synthesis Control
```
# Real-time synthesis parameters
puredata_manager("send_float", receiver="osc_freq", value=220.0)
puredata_manager("send_float", receiver="filter_q", value=0.8)
puredata_manager("send_bang", receiver="note_on")
```

### Interactive Installations
```
# Sensor integration
puredata_manager("send_float", receiver="proximity", value=sensor_value)
puredata_manager("send_bang", receiver="motion_trigger")
puredata_manager("send_float", receiver="light_level", value=light_sensor)
```

### Generative Systems
```
# Algorithmic composition
for pitch in melody:
    puredata_manager("send_float", receiver="pitch", value=pitch)
    puredata_manager("send_bang", receiver="play_note")
    time.sleep(note_duration)
```

## Pd Object Integration

### Common OSC Objects
- **oscparse:** Parse incoming OSC messages
- **oscroute:** Route OSC messages by address
- **oscformat:** Format outgoing OSC messages
- **udpreceive/send:** UDP network communication

### Signal Processing
- Audio synthesis objects (osc~, saw~, etc.)
- Effects processing (delread~, vd~, etc.)
- Control objects (line~, vline~, etc.)
- GUI objects (slider, toggle, etc.)

